WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:10.630
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the seventh of April. Can you all hear me, or am I talking to myself again?</v>

00:00:11.619 --> 00:00:21.070
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, we can hear you. Less cheerful news: the broken coffee machine in the canteen is still ruining my morning. Just a moan, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.859
<v David Whitfield>Thought you sounded a bit under-voltage.</v>

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.300
<v Callum Reid>There's a birthday cake in the office, though. Slightly makes up for it.</v>

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:38.229
<v Sarah Okafor>And the charity bake sale on Friday. Entire factory apparently runs on sponge. Right, enough catering.</v>

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.369
<v Jamie Brennan>Shame. Only bit of the meeting I was fully qualified for.</v>

00:00:45.159 --> 00:00:49.359
<v Fiona Doyle>Quick close-out from me: finished the repair on the wrapper last night.</v>

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. That's finished work, then, not something we're carrying into today.</v>

00:00:54.850 --> 00:01:00.100
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. Also tested the line 2 guard yesterday and it's all fine now. Both closed.</v>

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:06.170
<v Callum Reid>On nights, noticed the turbine one compressor was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.980
<v David Whitfield>Settled properly, yeah? Not just a dip on the trend?</v>

00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:21.180
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, back to normal. Same sort of thing with the line 1 mould temp — running a bit warm on nights, then it settled down. Just observations, those.</v>

00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:24.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. No new jobs off those two observations.</v>

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:35.239
<v Aisha Begum>And the shutdown on the line two is cancelled now, production need it running. So that one's off, not waiting for someone to pick it up.</v>

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.030
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, cancelled. We're not planning around a shutdown that isn't happening.</v>

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:50.280
<v David Whitfield>Other thing, I can't get to the main water valve until production gives us a window. Still blocked, nothing I can do on it at the minute.</v>

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:54.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, stays blocked. Not adding that to today's agreed work.</v>

00:01:55.230 --> 00:02:00.129
<v Fiona Doyle>Um, I'll inspect the relief valve for leaks. I'll drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:01.469 --> 00:02:06.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona. Inspect the relief valve for leaks, and yes, drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:08.719 --> 00:02:11.169
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that's mine. Inspection for leaks, understood.</v>

00:02:12.469 --> 00:02:17.719
<v Callum Reid>And separately we've got the boiler issue. That's the one stopping production at the moment.</v>

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:26.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya, can you replace the seals on the PRV on the boiler? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:33.439
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the PRV on the boiler. That's first for me.</v>

00:02:35.349 --> 00:02:41.650
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, talking over you — we're keeping that separate from the relief valve inspection, aren't we? Two jobs.</v>

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:48.979
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, separate. Mine's inspecting the relief valve for leaks, not the seals on the PRV on the boiler.</v>

00:02:50.009 --> 00:02:56.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Fiona drops everything for the inspection; Priya's seals job comes first for her because production's held up.</v>

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:05.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Davey, can you grease and check the bearings on the gas turbine two for Monday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:13.139
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the gas turbine two. Monday, got it. Won't let it drift.</v>

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.599
<v Callum Reid>That's gas turbine two, not the turbine one compressor I mentioned earlier.</v>

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:26.270
<v David Whitfield>Yep, gas turbine two. Yours settled down; this is the bearings job.</v>

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:36.069
<v Sarah Okafor>And David Whitfield, can you take vibration readings on the air compressor by Wednesday? Again, not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:37.039 --> 00:03:42.990
<v David Whitfield>I can, yeah. I'll take vibration readings on the air compressor by Wednesday. Understood on the priority.</v>

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.280
<v Priya Raman>Ooh, full name. You're in trouble now.</v>

00:03:46.979 --> 00:03:49.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Only making sure the right bloke's listening.</v>

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.229
<v David Whitfield>Both versions of me are here, unfortunately.</v>

00:03:56.389 --> 00:03:59.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team?</v>

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.699
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team. That's with me.</v>

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:11.110
<v Callum Reid>Good. Easy for that sort of thing to get lost underneath all the plant stuff.</v>

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.480
<v Jamie Brennan>Mm, agreed. Toolbox talk is mine, no ambiguity there.</v>

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:23.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you also run the monthly fire alarm test? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:30.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.379
<v Priya Raman>That'll be louder than this Teams audio, at least.</v>

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:41.019
<v Jamie Brennan>Low bar. Half of you sound like you're inside a biscuit tin.</v>

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:48.470
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha Begum, can you send the shift handover report round by 11am? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:49.829 --> 00:04:56.829
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round by 11am. Got it — not an emergency, still needs to land.</v>

00:04:57.850 --> 00:05:03.449
<v Callum Reid>Good, the handover report's useful. Stops us all working off slightly different versions of the shift.</v>

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.810
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. And just so nobody's confused, that doesn't mean the cancelled shutdown is back on.</v>

00:05:12.129 --> 00:05:15.279
<v Sarah Okafor>No, definitely not. Report goes round; shutdown stays cancelled.</v>

00:05:17.629 --> 00:05:23.930
<v Sarah Okafor>For mine, I'll do the pre-use checks on the trucks by end of day. Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:05:26.329 --> 00:05:33.329
<v Callum Reid>Right, Sarah's doing the trucks. They're parked, so nobody's treating 'by end of day' as permission to use them unchecked.</v>

00:05:34.399 --> 00:05:40.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. I'll do the pre-use checks, before use, by end of day. Fairly important, and that's mine.</v>

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:49.860
<v Callum Reid>We've still got to write up the near miss at the stretch wrapper by the end of the week. That hasn't got anyone against it.</v>

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:56.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, who can take the near-miss write-up? Anyone got room for that?</v>

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.790
<v David Whitfield>Not me, sorry. I can't take that on as well.</v>

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:06.639
<v Jamie Brennan>I haven't got room for it either, to be honest.</v>

00:06:08.379 --> 00:06:14.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, nobody's taking it. It still needs doing; I'm leaving it explicitly unowned, not pretending it's covered.</v>

00:06:16.079 --> 00:06:21.329
<v Fiona Doyle>And my finished wrapper repair isn't that write-up. Mechanical repair's done; the near-miss paperwork isn't.</v>

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:27.870
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, exactly. Repair completed doesn't close the near miss at the stretch wrapper.</v>

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Write-up needed by the end of the week, nobody assigned. That's the gap.</v>

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:42.930
<v Priya Raman>Clear on mine: replace the seals on the PRV on the boiler first, because that's holding production up.</v>

00:06:44.899 --> 00:06:50.500
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll drop everything for inspecting the relief valve for leaks. No muddling those two together.</v>

00:06:51.990 --> 00:07:01.790
<v David Whitfield>I've got grease and check the bearings on the gas turbine two for Monday, vibration readings on the air compressor by Wednesday. Neither an emergency, neither to slip.</v>

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:09.209
<v Jamie Brennan>Toolbox talk for the team and monthly fire alarm test with me. Heard the don't-let-it-slip bit on the test.</v>

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.600
<v Aisha Begum>Shift handover report round by 11am with me.</v>

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:22.019
<v Sarah Okafor>And pre-use checks on the trucks with me, by end of day. Right, that's the agreed work and the unowned write-up made clear.</v>

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.750
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. Back to my entirely theoretical coffee.</v>

00:07:28.329 --> 00:07:30.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Living the dream. Cheers, everyone.</v>
